{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01025",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.88,
      "end_seconds": 5.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "Hi, doctor, I hope I'm not disturbing you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.61,
      "end_seconds": 14.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "You're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 16.53,
      "end_seconds": 20.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Thank you for fitting us in, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.51,
      "end_seconds": 24.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Please do. Extra information is always welcome."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.83,
      "end_seconds": 28.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "It's burning when I pass urine, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.32,
      "end_seconds": 30.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.56,
      "end_seconds": 43.7,
      "duration_seconds": 12.14,
      "text": "Honestly I can't say exactly when it started. It might have been last month or the month before, I really can't pin it down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.75,
      "end_seconds": 50.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.26,
      "end_seconds": 55.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "It happens a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.56,
      "end_seconds": 58.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.73,
      "end_seconds": 69.79,
      "duration_seconds": 9.06,
      "text": "Erm, uh, when it starts I tend to get a dull ache low in my tummy as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.76,
      "end_seconds": 77.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.17,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 78.03,
      "end_seconds": 83.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.37,
      "end_seconds": 86.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.56,
      "end_seconds": 92.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.11,
      "end_seconds": 96.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "It feels mild to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.5,
      "end_seconds": 101.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Have you been going to the toilet often?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.59,
      "end_seconds": 111.73,
      "duration_seconds": 9.14,
      "text": "Yeah. Six months, I'd say. Mm, uh, with going to the toilet often, it feels severe to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.51,
      "end_seconds": 116.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.74,
      "end_seconds": 128.19,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "Yes, I had my appendix taken out, when I was in my twenties."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.73,
      "end_seconds": 134.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "Alright, tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.16,
      "end_seconds": 150.58,
      "duration_seconds": 14.42,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours. No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.41,
      "end_seconds": 157.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.61,
      "end_seconds": 166.69,
      "duration_seconds": 8.08,
      "text": "It's hydrocortisone cream, when needed. Escitalopram. I take it 10 milligrams, maybe, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.39,
      "end_seconds": 173.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Do you have the packet or the prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.09,
      "end_seconds": 181.24,
      "duration_seconds": 7.15,
      "text": "No, it's at home. I had levetiracetam at one point, but I'm off it now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.03,
      "end_seconds": 187.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Right, does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.35,
      "end_seconds": 190.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "My grandmother had dementia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.35,
      "end_seconds": 194.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.96,
      "end_seconds": 203.84,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "I have eczema, for five years. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.59,
      "end_seconds": 206.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "Hm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.41,
      "end_seconds": 230.98,
      "duration_seconds": 23.57,
      "text": "I have epilepsy. I told my wife I'd come today. I've got depression. I've been reading about it online and it worried me. I thought it would sort itself out, you know, but it hasn't. I've had anxiety for five years now. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.23,
      "end_seconds": 238.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "Okay, I can see eczema and depression in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.29,
      "end_seconds": 255.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any blood in the urine, vaginal discharge or back pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.2,
      "end_seconds": 258.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "No, I'd have said so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.91,
      "end_seconds": 261.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Nothing like fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.05,
      "end_seconds": 263.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "No, no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 264.77,
      "end_seconds": 269.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.18,
      "end_seconds": 277.48,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.23,
      "end_seconds": 287.41,
      "duration_seconds": 8.18,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. On the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.32,
      "end_seconds": 295.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.3,
      "end_seconds": 301.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.85,
      "end_seconds": 303.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Nothing odd there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.08,
      "end_seconds": 307.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.12,
      "end_seconds": 320.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.13,
      "end_seconds": 340.85,
      "duration_seconds": 7.72,
      "text": "Okay: SpO2 98 percent on room air, pulse 86. And respiratory rate 14, BP is 128 over 69."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.76,
      "end_seconds": 346.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.14,
      "end_seconds": 349.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.18,
      "end_seconds": 369.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft with slight tenderness just above the pubic bone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.9,
      "end_seconds": 375.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "You can relax now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 394.12,
      "end_seconds": 402.5,
      "duration_seconds": 8.38,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. My working impression is an uncomplicated urinary infection. I'd also keep vaginal irritation in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 404.42,
      "end_seconds": 407.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 408.23,
      "end_seconds": 423.57,
      "duration_seconds": 15.34,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's an uncomplicated urinary infection, and we'll know more once the a urine dipstick is back. I'm going to order a urine dipstick, for burning urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 424.46,
      "end_seconds": 426.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "The earliest is Thursday, 10 am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 428.74,
      "end_seconds": 446.49,
      "duration_seconds": 17.75,
      "text": "We'll begin with nitrofurantoin, 100 milligrams, twice a day, three days. It's for urinary infection. Drink plenty of water and avoid holding urine. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 447.91,
      "end_seconds": 451.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Okay, I'll look out for that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 453.08,
      "end_seconds": 472.6,
      "duration_seconds": 19.52,
      "text": "Please don't wait if you get a fever or back pain. That's when to be seen urgently. Come back if it is not better in three days. Can you tell me the plan back in your own words, so I know I've explained it clearly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 478.89,
      "end_seconds": 490.42,
      "duration_seconds": 11.53,
      "text": "So, I take the nitrofurantoin, 100 milligrams, twice a day and come back if it is not better in three days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 495.6,
      "end_seconds": 501.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 502.26,
      "end_seconds": 504.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 505.49,
      "end_seconds": 506.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
}